<div class="panel"><h3 id="glyph-title"></h3><p id="glyph-construction"></p><p id="glyph-source" class="note"></p><div class="callout" id="glyph-note"></div><h3 style="margin-top:1rem">Starts, stops and landmarks</h3><div id="stroke-list"></div><details open><summary>Construction and geometric joint reads</summary><p class="note">Construction reads use the ordered strokes: a later outward branch and an arriving stop can have the same final geometry. Site numbers are local references. Geometry is shown separately, and does not establish a traffic law.</p><div class="data-scroll" id="joint-table"></div></details><details><summary>Sections and shared sites</summary><p class="note">Select a row to highlight its section. Concentric rings mark distinct sites at the same displayed position.</p><div class="data-scroll" id="section-table"></div></details></div></div>
<details class="compare" id="compare"><summary>Compare a second construction of this glyph</summary><div class="toolbar"><label class="grow">Other construction <select id="comparison-select" aria-label="Comparison construction"></select></label></div><div class="split"><div class="panel"><h3 id="compare-title"></h3><div id="compare-art"></div></div><div class="panel"><p id="compare-description"></p><div class="callout limit" id="compare-note"></div><p class="note">Matching pictures do not establish the same history, connectivity or future permissions. This view displays the supplied alternatives; it does not infer an equivalence.</p></div></div></details>
</section>
<section class="section" id="machines"><div class="kicker">02 / A joint becomes a machine through use</div><h2>Same lines, different permitted routes</h2><p>A probe offers material participation at an exposed port. The native rule supplies allowed routes; unresolved alternatives remain possibilities. It does not send the same packet down every branch.</p><p class="note">Transfers here are atomic from input to output port. Interior sites certify path connectivity; travel time, impact and residence at those sites are not simulated.</p><div class="machine-menu" id="machine-menu"></div><div class="split"><div class="panel"><h3 id="machine-title"></h3><div id="machine-art"></div><div class="legend"><span><i class="dot"></i>Structure</span><span><i class="dot" style="background:var(--gold)"></i>Selected candidate routes</span><span><i class="dot" style="background:var(--rose)"></i>Input</span></div><p id="machine-construction"></p></div><div class="panel"><h3>What the joint permits</h3><p id="machine-use"></p><div class="data-scroll" id="probe-table"></div><div class="probe-detail callout" id="probe-detail"></div><p class="callout limit" id="machine-limit"></p><details><summary>Explicit routes</summary><div id="route-table" class="data-scroll"></div></details></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="contexts"><div class="kicker">03 / A frame makes a different question possible</div><h2>Ground, contact and a possible use</h2><p>A and V suggest different support arrangements once ground and a load are supplied. Here we ask a narrower question: where does that load project relative to the selected contact span?</p><div class="context-menu" id="context-menu"></div><div class="split"><div class="panel"><h3 id="context-title"></h3><div id="context-art"></div><div class="legend"><span><i class="dot" style="background:var(--gold)"></i>Selected ground</span><span><i class="dot"></i>Declared contact</span><span><i class="dot" style="background:var(--rose)"></i>Load and projection</span></div></div><div class="panel"><div id="context-result"></div><p id="context-construction"></p><p class="context-interpretation" id="context-interpretation"></p><div class="callout limit" id="context-limit"></div><p class="note">Inside is a conditional geometric read. It is not a stability verdict: material, rigidity, friction, load distribution, out-of-plane support and dynamics are not supplied by a glyph outline.</p></div></div><h3 style="margin-top:1.6rem">A small vocabulary of possible uses</h3><p class="note">These transfer sketches identify a reusable relation and the extra context needed. The noun labels are explanations; they do not execute the mechanism.</p><div id="transfer-grid" class="transfer-grid"></div></section>
<section class="section" id="encoding"><div class="kicker">04 / What the encoding carries</div><h2>Keep the evidence connected</h2><div class="reading"><p>The glyph name is not an instruction. Native section endpoints, ordered visits, ports and laws carry the distinctions. A reader can inspect one level while leaving another open.</p><div class="data-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Surface</th><th>What connects to what</th><th>What remains separate</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Section</td><td>Actual start site → actual end site, with geometric evidence</td><td>Equal positions do not weld sites.</td></tr><tr><td>Pen stroke</td><td>An ordered sequence of section visits, each with traversal</td><td>A lift changes history, not automatically the finished topology.</td></tr><tr><td>Construction landmark</td><td>A start or stop linked to an earlier exposed site, or a declared relative placement</td><td>Later ink cannot supply evidence for an earlier move.</td></tr><tr><td>Joint</td><td>Several section ends use the same actual site</td><td>Attachment does not prescribe traffic or branch allocation.</td></tr><tr><td>Route</td><td>Exposed input → connected passage → exposed destination</td><td>Being drawable is not permission to transfer.</td></tr><tr><td>Conditional law</td><td>Input and control → possible route selections</td><td>A set of possibilities is not several material executions.</td></tr><tr><td>Ground read</td><td>Shape + selected ground + contacts + load → projection evidence</td><td>The result is conditional on the supplied basis and premises.</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Source → chosen parts, with retained correspondence</td><td>Omitting a part from a read does not erase it or stop its flow.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><strong>ODV still describes the selected magnitude read.</strong> V = 0 means undetectable at that resolution. It does not mean a missing section or an unselected stroke. Here a joint needs connected sites and laws; it is not compressed into one new joint bit.</p><div class="callout">A bend and an attachment may have identical final ink and connectivity. Their difference survives only if the construction history or different response laws survive. The same applies to a bridge that was drawn in one direction but is later usable in both.</div><p class="note">Pen-stroke groups record drawing history. They do not supply material stiffness or bolt, hinge or weld laws.</p><h3 style="margin-top:1.4rem">What this pass does not establish</h3><p>It does not discover handwriting plans, learn meanings from images, certify mechanical balance, or supply a universal workspace or force solver. It gives concrete native structures, executed finite route probes and explicit counterexamples that a later learner can compare.</p><p>Uses and interactions can broaden a concept beyond its isolated outline. That is a useful direction for Gojo; a complete concept is not guaranteed by collecting a list of associations.</p><div class="links"><a href="README.md">Full Markdown equivalent</a><a href="results.json">Recorded JSON</a><a href="corpus.gojo">Glyph native archive</a><a href="construction.gojo">Construction landmark archive</a><a href="usage.gojo">Route native archive</a><a href="contexts.gojo">Context native archive</a></div></div></section>
<footer class="footer">Gojo · Glyph joint atlas · Authored examples and recorded native reads. Colors, labels and screen coordinates are presentation aids.</footer></main>
<script id="study-data" type="application/json">@@DATA@@</script><script>
'use strict';
const data=JSON.parse(document.getElementById('study-data').textContent);
const corpus=Array.isArray(data.Corpus)?data.Corpus:(data.Corpus?.Fixtures||[]), cases=data.Usage?.Cases||[], contexts=data.Contexts?.Cases||[];
const $=id=>document.getElementById(id), esc=s=>String(s??'').replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]));
const colors=['#157e79','#b43e64','#4666b5','#a66a16','#7654ad','#527c30'];
const glyphs=[...new Set(corpus.map(x=>x.Glyph))], state={glyph:0,variant:0,stroke:-1,section:-1,machine:0,probe:0,context:0};
const point=p=>Array.isArray(p)?{x:Number(p[0]),y:Number(p[1])}:{x:Number(p.X??p.x),y:Number(p.Y??p.y)};
const xy=p=>`${p.x},${-p.y}`;
const current=()=>corpus.filter(x=>x.Glyph===glyphs[state.glyph])[state.variant];
const variants=()=>corpus.filter(x=>x.Glyph===glyphs[state.glyph]);
function path(points){const p=points.map(point);if(!p.length)return '';const c=p.slice(1).map(xy).join(' ');return `M${xy(p[0])} ${p.length===2?'L':p.length===3?'Q':p.length===4?'C':'L'}${c}`;}
function bounds(points,padding=.9){const ps=points.map(point).filter(p=>Number.isFinite(p.x)&&Number.isFinite(p.y));if(!ps.length)return '-1 -11 10 12';const x=Math.min(...ps.map(p=>p.x)),xx=Math.max(...ps.map(p=>p.x)),y=Math.min(...ps.map(p=>p.y)),yy=Math.max(...ps.map(p=>p.y));return `${x-padding} ${-yy-padding} ${Math.max(1,xx-x)+2*padding} ${Math.max(1,yy-y)+2*padding}`;}
function svg(content,points,{cls='art',label='',id='view',padding=1}={}){return `<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="${cls}" role="img" aria-label="${esc(label)}" viewBox="${bounds(points,padding)}"><defs><marker id="${id}-arrow" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="6" refY="4" markerWidth="4" markerHeight="4" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8 Z" fill="context-stroke"/></marker></defs>${content}</svg>`;}
function curveReverse(p){return p.slice().reverse();}
function strokeEnds(f,s){if(!s?.Visits?.length)return null;const a=s.Visits[0],b=s.Visits.at(-1),first=f.Lines.find(l=>l.Index===a.Section),last=f.Lines.find(l=>l.Index===b.Section);if(!first||!last)return null;return {start:point(a.Reverse?first.Controls.at(-1):first.Controls[0]),end:point(b.Reverse?last.Controls[0]:last.Controls.at(-1)),startSite:a.Reverse?first.EndSite:first.StartSite,endSite:b.Reverse?last.StartSite:last.EndSite};}
const strokeRefs=values=>(values||[]).length?(values||[]).map(i=>Number(i)+1).join(', '):'none';
const strokeRead=(f,index)=>(f.ConstructionRead?.Strokes||[]).find(s=>s.Index===index);
function teachingReference(f){return f.SourceUrl?`Teaching reference: <a href="${esc(f.SourceUrl)}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">${esc(f.SourceTitle||'Formation guide')}</a>`:'';}
function glyphSvg(f,{id='glyph',small=false,stroke=-1,section=-1,sites=false,direction=false,lifts=false}={}){
 if(!f)return '<div class="empty">No construction supplied.</div>';
 const width=small ? .34 : .16, all=f.Lines.flatMap(x=>x.Controls), owner=new Map();
 f.Strokes.forEach((s,i)=>s.Visits.forEach(v=>{if(!owner.has(v.Section))owner.set(v.Section,i);}));
 let content='';
 for(const line of f.Lines){const i=owner.get(line.Index)??0, selected=(stroke<0||f.Strokes[stroke]?.Visits.some(v=>v.Section===line.Index))&&(section<0||section===line.Index), color=small?'currentColor':colors[(selected&&stroke>=0?stroke:i)%colors.length],opacity=selected?1:stroke>=0?(i<stroke ? .42 : .07):.16;content+=`<path d="${path(line.Controls)}" fill="none" stroke="${color}" stroke-width="${width}" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" opacity="${opacity}"/>`;}
 if(direction&&!small){f.Strokes.forEach((s,i)=>{if(stroke>=0&&stroke!==i)return;s.Visits.forEach(v=>{const line=f.Lines.find(l=>l.Index===v.Section);if(!line||section>=0&&section!==line.Index)return;const pts=(v.Reverse?curveReverse(line.Controls):line.Controls).map(point),at=.57,dt=.045;function atT(t){if(pts.length===2)return{x:pts[0].x*(1-t)+pts[1].x*t,y:pts[0].y*(1-t)+pts[1].y*t};let q=pts.map(p=>({...p}));while(q.length>1)q=q.slice(0,-1).map((p,j)=>({x:p.x*(1-t)+q[j+1].x*t,y:p.y*(1-t)+q[j+1].y*t}));return q[0];}const a=atT(at-dt),b=atT(at);content+=`<path d="M${xy(a)} L${xy(b)}" stroke="${colors[i%colors.length]}" stroke-width=".13" fill="none" marker-end="url(#${id}-arrow)"/>`;});});}
 if(lifts&&!small){for(let i=1;i<f.Strokes.length;i++){if(stroke>=0&&stroke!==i)continue;const previous=strokeEnds(f,f.Strokes[i-1]),next=strokeEnds(f,f.Strokes[i]);if(!previous||!next)continue;const evidence=strokeRead(f,i);content+=`<path class="landmark-move" d="M${xy(previous.end)} L${xy(next.start)}" stroke="#889a96" stroke-width=".07" stroke-dasharray=".15 .15" fill="none"><title>Lift, then move to stroke ${i+1} start: ${esc(evidence?.StartDescription||'start landmark not supplied')}</title></path>`;}}
 if(sites&&!small){for(const s of f.Sites){const p=point(s),coincident=f.Sites.filter(t=>t.X===s.X&&t.Y===s.Y),offset=coincident.indexOf(s),r=(s.Degree>2?.18:.12)+offset*.09,fill=coincident.length>1?'none':s.Degree===1?'#fffefa':s.Degree>2?'#b43e64':'#157e79';content+=`<circle cx="${p.x}" cy="${-p.y}" r="${r}" fill="${fill}" stroke="#20343a" stroke-width=".045"/><text x="${p.x+.22}" y="${-p.y-.2-offset*.34}" font-size=".29" fill="#486169">p${s.Index}${coincident.length>1?' (distinct)':''}</text>`;}}
 if(!small){f.Strokes.forEach((s,i)=>{if(stroke>=0&&stroke!==i)return;const ends=strokeEnds(f,s);if(!ends)return;const history=strokeRead(f,i);content+=`<circle class="stroke-start" data-stroke="${i}" cx="${ends.start.x}" cy="${-ends.start.y}" r=".24" fill="none" stroke="#30954a" stroke-width=".09"><title>Stroke ${i+1} starts at p${ends.startSite}: ${esc(history?.StartDescription||'start')}</title></circle><circle class="stroke-stop" data-stroke="${i}" cx="${ends.end.x}" cy="${-ends.end.y}" r=".115" fill="#ce493c" stroke="#fffefa" stroke-width=".025"><title>Stroke ${i+1} stops at p${ends.endSite}: ${esc(history?.EndDescription||'stop')}</title></circle>`;});}
 return svg(content,all,{id,cls:small?'':'art',label:`${f.Glyph}: ${f.Title}`,padding:small ? .7 : 1.05});
}
function glyphGrid(){ $('glyph-grid').innerHTML=glyphs.map((g,i)=>`<button class="tile" data-glyph="${i}" aria-label="${esc(g)}" aria-pressed="${i===state.glyph}">${glyphSvg(corpus.find(f=>f.Glyph===g),{small:true,id:'tile'+i})}<span>${esc(g)}</span></button>`).join('');$('glyph-grid').querySelectorAll('button').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>selectGlyph(+b.dataset.glyph));}
function selectGlyph(i){state.glyph=(i+glyphs.length)%glyphs.length;state.variant=0;state.stroke=-1;state.section=-1;$('glyph-select').value=state.glyph;fillVariants();renderGlyph();glyphGrid();}
function fillVariants(){const vs=variants();$('variant-select').innerHTML=vs.map((f,i)=>`<option value="${i}">${esc(f.Title)}</option>`).join('');$('comparison-select').innerHTML=vs.map((f,i)=>`<option value="${i}">${esc(f.Title)}</option>`).join('');$('comparison-select').value=vs.length>1?(state.variant+1)%vs.length:0;$('compare').hidden=vs.length<2;}
function renderGlyph(){const f=current();if(!f)return;$('variant-select').value=state.variant;$('glyph-art').innerHTML=glyphSvg(f,{id:'main',stroke:state.stroke,section:state.section,sites:$('show-sites').checked,direction:$('show-direction').checked,lifts:$('show-lifts').checked});$('glyph-title').textContent=`${f.Glyph} · ${f.Title}`;$('glyph-construction').textContent=f.Construction;$('glyph-note').textContent=f.Note;$('glyph-note').hidden=!f.Note;$('glyph-source').innerHTML=teachingReference(f);$('glyph-source').hidden=!f.SourceUrl;
 const t=f.Topology;$('glyph-stats').innerHTML=[['components',t.Components],['free ends',t.FreeEnds],['branch sites',t.Branches],['independent cycles',t.CycleRank],['pen strokes',t.PenStrokes],['revisits',t.RevisitedSections]].map(([label,value])=>`<span class="stat"><strong>${value}</strong>${label}</span>`).join('')+(!t.Complete?'<span class="badge unknown">incomplete read</span>':'')+(f.ConstructionRead?.Complete===false?'<span class="badge unknown">incomplete construction history</span>':'');
 $('stroke-controls').innerHTML=`<button data-stroke="-1" aria-pressed="${state.stroke<0}">All strokes</button>`+f.Strokes.map((s,i)=>`<button data-stroke="${i}" aria-pressed="${state.stroke===i}" style="${state.stroke===i?'background:'+colors[i%colors.length]+';border-color:'+colors[i%colors.length]:''}">Stroke ${i+1}</button>`).join('');$('stroke-controls').querySelectorAll('button').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{state.stroke=+b.dataset.stroke;state.section=-1;renderGlyph();});
 const currentRead=strokeRead(f,state.stroke);$('selected-stroke').innerHTML=currentRead?`<strong>Stroke ${state.stroke+1}: p${currentRead.StartSite} → p${currentRead.EndSite}</strong><p>Start: ${esc(currentRead.StartDescription)}</p><p>Stop: ${esc(currentRead.EndDescription)}</p><small>Earlier ink remains visible; later ink is faint. Dashed movement is a lifted pen, not a connecting stroke.</small>`:'Select a stroke to inspect its start, stop and earlier landmark evidence. Green rings mark starts; red dots mark stops.';
 $('stroke-list').innerHTML=f.Strokes.map((s,i)=>{const r=strokeRead(f,i),ends=strokeEnds(f,s),placement=r?.PlacementSourceStroke!=null?`<p class="note">Declared placement from p${r.PlacementSourceSite??'?'} on stroke ${r.PlacementSourceStroke+1}: local offset (${esc((r.PlacementOffset||[]).join(', '))}); parallel read: ${r.ParallelToSource===null?'unresolved':r.ParallelToSource?'yes':'no'}.</p>`:'';return `<article class="stroke-card ${state.stroke===i?'active':''}"><button data-inspect-stroke="${i}" aria-pressed="${state.stroke===i}">Stroke ${i+1}</button> <span class="badge">${s.Closed?'closed':s.Continuous?'continuous':'not continuous'}</span><p><strong class="start-label">Start p${r?.StartSite??ends?.startSite??'?'}</strong> — ${esc(r?.StartDescription||'construction read not supplied')}</p><p><strong class="stop-label">Stop p${r?.EndSite??ends?.endSite??'?'}</strong> — ${esc(r?.EndDescription||'construction read not supplied')}</p>${placement}<p class="tiny muted">Earlier ink at this start: stroke(s) ${strokeRefs(r?.StartSourceStrokes)}. Earlier ink at this stop: stroke(s) ${strokeRefs(r?.EndSourceStrokes)}.</p><details><summary>Ordered visits and construction events</summary><p class="tiny">${s.Visits.map(v=>`s${v.Section}${v.Reverse?' reversed':''}`).join(' → ')}</p>${(r?.Events||[]).map(e=>`<p class="note">p${e.Site}: ${esc(e.Description)}</p>`).join('')}</details></article>`;}).join('');$('stroke-list').querySelectorAll('[data-inspect-stroke]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{state.stroke=+b.dataset.inspectStroke;state.section=-1;renderGlyph();});
 $('section-table').innerHTML=`<table><thead><tr><th>Section</th><th>Actual endpoints</th><th>Geometry read</th></tr></thead><tbody>${f.Lines.map(l=>`<tr data-section="${l.Index}" class="${state.section===l.Index?'active':''}" tabindex="0" aria-label="Highlight section ${l.Index}"><td>s${l.Index}</td><td>p${l.StartSite} → p${l.EndSite}</td><td>${l.Straight===null?'unresolved':l.Straight?'straight':'curved'}</td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table>`;$('section-table').querySelectorAll('tr[data-section]').forEach(row=>{const act=()=>{state.section=state.section===+row.dataset.section?-1:+row.dataset.section;renderGlyph();};row.onclick=act;row.onkeydown=e=>{if(e.key==='Enter'||e.key===' '){e.preventDefault();act();}};});
 $('joint-table').innerHTML=`<table><thead><tr><th>Site</th><th>Construction history</th><th>Geometry only</th></tr></thead><tbody>${f.Sites.map(s=>{const history=(f.ConstructionRead?.Strokes||[]).flatMap(r=>(r.Events||[]).filter(e=>e.Site===s.Index).map(e=>({stroke:r.Index,description:e.Description})));return `<tr><td>p${s.Index}<br><small>${s.Degree} incidences</small></td><td>${history.length?history.map(e=>`<p class="tiny"><strong>Stroke ${e.stroke+1}:</strong> ${esc(e.description)}</p>`).join(''):'Unresolved construction read'}</td><td><span class="badge">${esc(s.Joint==='bend'?'corner geometry':s.Joint||'not supplied')}</span></td></tr>`;}).join('')}</tbody></table>`;renderCompare();}
function renderCompare(){const f=variants()[+$('comparison-select').value]||current();if(!f)return;$('compare-title').textContent=f.Title;$('compare-art').innerHTML=glyphSvg(f,{id:'compare-artifact',direction:true,sites:true});$('compare-description').textContent=f.Construction;$('compare-note').textContent=f.Note;}
function routeSvg(c,probe){const points=c.Points.map(point),byId=new Map(c.Points.map(p=>[p.Id,p]));let content='';for(const l of c.Lines){const a=byId.get(l.From),b=byId.get(l.To);if(a&&b)content+=`<path d="M${xy(point(a))} L${xy(point(b))}" stroke="${colors[(l.Stroke||0)%colors.length]}" stroke-width=".16" fill="none" opacity=".6"/>`;}
 const candidateIds=new Set(probe?.Candidates||[]);for(const r of c.Routes){if(!candidateIds.has(r.Id))continue;const route=[r.From,...r.Via,r.To].map(x=>byId.get(x)).filter(Boolean).map(point);if(route.length>1)content+=`<polyline points="${route.map(xy).join(' ')}" stroke="#b0781c" fill="none" stroke-width=".11" stroke-dasharray="${probe?.Outcome==='moved'?'none':'.18 .12'}" marker-end="url(#route-arrow)"/>`;}
 for(const p of c.Points){const q=point(p),selected=(probe?.Input||'').split(' + ').includes(p.Id),coincident=c.Points.filter(t=>t.X===p.X&&t.Y===p.Y),offset=coincident.indexOf(p);content+=`<circle cx="${q.x}" cy="${-q.y}" r="${(selected ? .19 : .12)+offset*.09}" fill="${coincident.length>1?'none':selected?'#b43e64':'#fffefa'}" stroke="${selected?'#b43e64':'#344e51'}" stroke-width=".05"/><text x="${q.x+.23}" y="${-q.y-.2-offset*.34}" font-size=".29" fill="#344e51">${esc(p.Label||p.Id)}</text>`;}
 return svg(content,points,{label:c.Title,id:'route',padding:1.05});}
function renderMachine(){const c=cases[state.machine];if(!c)return;$('machine-menu').innerHTML=cases.map((x,i)=>`<button data-machine="${i}" aria-pressed="${i===state.machine}">${esc(x.Title)}</button>`).join('');$('machine-menu').querySelectorAll('button').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{state.machine=+b.dataset.machine;state.probe=0;renderMachine();});const p=c.Probes[state.probe];$('machine-title').textContent=c.Title;$('machine-art').innerHTML=routeSvg(c,p);$('machine-construction').textContent=c.Construction;$('machine-use').textContent=c.Use;$('machine-limit').textContent=c.Limits;$('probe-table').innerHTML=`<table><thead><tr><th>Probe</th><th>Input / control</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody>${c.Probes.map((x,i)=>`<tr class="route-row ${i===state.probe?'active':''}" data-probe="${i}" tabindex="0"><td>${esc(x.Id)}</td><td>${esc(x.Input)}<br><span class="muted">${esc(x.Controls.join(', ')||'no supplied control')}</span></td><td><span class="badge ${esc(x.Outcome)}">${esc(x.Outcome)}</span></td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table>`;$('probe-table').querySelectorAll('[data-probe]').forEach(row=>{const act=()=>{state.probe=+row.dataset.probe;renderMachine();};row.onclick=act;row.onkeydown=e=>{if(e.key==='Enter'||e.key===' '){e.preventDefault();act();}};});$('probe-detail').innerHTML=p?`<strong>${esc(p.Explanation)}</strong><p class="mono">${p.Incoming} incoming = ${p.Accepted} accepted + ${p.Blocked} blocked + ${p.Remainder} remainder</p><span class="note">Candidates: ${esc(p.Candidates.join(', ')||'none')}. Destination: ${esc(p.Destinations.join(', ')||'no move')}. Ownership ${p.OwnershipPreserved?'preserved':'not established'}.</span>`:'No probe supplied.';$('route-table').innerHTML=`<table><thead><tr><th>Route</th><th>From</th><th>Via</th><th>To</th></tr></thead><tbody>${c.Routes.map(r=>`<tr><td>${esc(r.Id)}</td><td>${esc(r.From)}</td><td>${esc(r.Via.join(' → '))}</td><td>${esc(r.To)}</td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table>`;}
function contextSvg(c){let content='',points=c.Lines.flat();for(const l of c.Lines)content+=`<path d="${path(l)}" stroke="#344f55" stroke-width=".15" fill="none" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round"/>`;if(c.Ground?.length===2){points.push(...c.Ground);content+=`<path d="${path(c.Ground)}" stroke="#ae7b2f" stroke-width=".12" fill="none"/>`;}for(const contact of c.Contacts||[]){const p=point(contact);points.push(contact);content+=`<circle cx="${p.x}" cy="${-p.y}" r=".2" fill="#157e79" stroke="#fffefa" stroke-width=".07"/>`;}if(c.Load?.length===2){const a=point(c.Load);points.push(c.Load);content+=`<circle cx="${a.x}" cy="${-a.y}" r=".16" fill="#b43e64"/>`;if(c.Projection?.length===2){const b=point(c.Projection);points.push(c.Projection);content+=`<path d="M${xy(a)} L${xy(b)}" stroke="#b43e64" stroke-width=".085" stroke-dasharray=".15 .1" fill="none" marker-end="url(#context-arrow)"/><circle cx="${b.x}" cy="${-b.y}" r=".16" fill="#fffefa" stroke="#b43e64" stroke-width=".075"/>`;}}
 return svg(content,points,{label:c.Title,id:'context',padding:1.1});}
function renderContext(){const c=contexts[state.context];if(!c)return;$('context-menu').innerHTML=contexts.map((x,i)=>`<button data-context="${i}" aria-pressed="${i===state.context}">${esc(x.Title)}</button>`).join('');$('context-menu').querySelectorAll('button').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{state.context=+b.dataset.context;renderContext();});$('context-title').textContent=c.Title;$('context-art').innerHTML=contextSvg(c);$('context-result').innerHTML=`<span class="badge ${esc(c.ProjectionRead)}">Projection: ${esc(c.ProjectionRead)}</span><div class="stats"><span class="stat">${(c.Contacts||[]).length} supplied contacts</span><span class="stat">${c.ContactCount} validated contacts</span><span class="stat">${c.NativeComplete?'complete selected read':'incomplete selected read'}</span></div>`;$('context-construction').textContent=c.Construction;$('context-interpretation').textContent=c.Interpretation;$('context-limit').textContent=c.Limits;}
function keepArrowFocus(select,change){select.addEventListener('keydown',e=>{if(!['ArrowLeft','ArrowRight','ArrowUp','ArrowDown'].includes(e.key))return;e.preventDefault();const n=select.options.length;if(!n)return;select.selectedIndex=(select.selectedIndex+(['ArrowLeft','ArrowUp'].includes(e.key)?-1:1)+n)%n;change();select.focus({preventScroll:true});});}
 $('glyph-select').innerHTML=glyphs.map((g,i)=>`<option value="${i}">${esc(g)}</option>`).join('');$('corpus-count').textContent=`${glyphs.length} glyphs · ${corpus.length} supplied constructions`;
$('glyph-select').onchange=()=>selectGlyph(+$('glyph-select').value);keepArrowFocus($('glyph-select'),()=>selectGlyph(+$('glyph-select').value));
function variantChange(){state.variant=+$('variant-select').value;state.stroke=-1;state.section=-1;if(+$('comparison-select').value===state.variant&&variants().length>1)$('comparison-select').value=(state.variant+1)%variants().length;renderGlyph();}$('variant-select').onchange=variantChange;keepArrowFocus($('variant-select'),variantChange);
$('comparison-select').onchange=renderCompare;keepArrowFocus($('comparison-select'),renderCompare);
$('previous').onclick=()=>selectGlyph(state.glyph-1);$('next').onclick=()=>selectGlyph(state.glyph+1);$('large-glyph').onclick=()=>selectGlyph(state.glyph+1);['show-sites','show-direction','show-lifts'].forEach(id=>$(id).onchange=renderGlyph);
$('transfer-grid').innerHTML=(data.Contexts?.Transfers||[]).map(t=>`<article class="transfer"><h3>${esc(t.Name)}</h3><div class="kicker">${esc(Array.isArray(t.Glyphs)?t.Glyphs.join(' · '):t.Glyphs)}</div><p>${esc(t.Structure)}</p><p><strong>Use:</strong> ${esc(t.Use)}</p><p><strong>Needs:</strong> ${esc(t.Needs)}</p><small>${esc(t.Limit)}</small></article>`).join('');
if(glyphs.length)selectGlyph(0);renderMachine();renderContext();
</script></body></html>
""";
}
